<Project>

  <!--
    The overlay worker is a sibling executable rather than a library, because
    general overlay cannot be interrupted in-process and has to be killable
    (Q-97, ADR-022 §9, benchmarks/geometry-overlay). Whoever needs to RUN it —
    the host, and the tests that prove the deadline works — needs its whole
    dependency closure in a directory beside them.

    Opt in with <CopyOverlayWorker>true</CopyOverlayWorker>. Defined here rather
    than duplicated in two project files so the two cannot drift; the first
    version lived only in the host, and every pool test failed with "the overlay
    worker is not at ..." because the test assembly runs from its own directory.
  -->
  <Target Name="CopyOverlayWorker"
          AfterTargets="Build"
          Condition="'$(CopyOverlayWorker)' == 'true'">
    <ItemGroup>
      <OverlayWorkerFiles
        Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)src\Graticula.Overlay.Worker\bin\$(Configuration)\$(TargetFramework)\**\*" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <Copy SourceFiles="@(OverlayWorkerFiles)"
          DestinationFolder="$(OutDir)overlay\%(RecursiveDir)"
          SkipUnchangedFiles="true" />
  </Target>

  <!--
    The geodatabase reader is the same arrangement for a different reason. The overlay worker is a
    separate process because OverlayNG cannot be interrupted; this one is because GDAL parses a file
    somebody else chose, and ADR-009 §2.2's words for keeping it out of the serving process are that it
    "removes an untrusted-file parser from the process that serves public requests" (ADR-037 §5a, D-88).

    Opt in with <CopyImportReader>true</CopyImportReader>.

    <b>It is much larger than the overlay worker and that is worth knowing before you wait for it.</b>
    MaxRev.Gdal's Windows and Linux runtime payloads are both restored, so the directory copied here
    carries two platforms' native libraries. SkipUnchangedFiles makes the second build cheap; the first
    is not, and a clean build of anything that opts in pays it.
  -->
  <Target Name="CopyImportReader"
          AfterTargets="Build"
          Condition="'$(CopyImportReader)' == 'true'">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ImportReaderFiles
        Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)src\Graticula.Import.Reader\bin\$(Configuration)\$(TargetFramework)\**\*" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <Copy SourceFiles="@(ImportReaderFiles)"
          DestinationFolder="$(OutDir)importer\%(RecursiveDir)"
          SkipUnchangedFiles="true" />
  </Target>

</Project>
